s checkpoint. No `commit_ack` supplied.\n\n## The `repository_delta=empty` question\n\nNot a no-op. The CR base OID `150040f` **is** the branch head, so base tree == candidate tree == HEAD tree == `7fce177` — the producer committed before the snapshot was taken. The real delta is `main..HEAD` = one signed, verified commit, 7 files, +609/-55. That commit is what I reviewed. The commit-owning mover should treat `main..HEAD` as this leaf's scope.\n\n## Attack, not reading\n\n- **Reachability grepped.** `admitSSHArguments` has one caller (`validateMesh:465`), reached from `validateConfiguration:391` via all four paths that can carry `ssh_args` (`validation.go:53,77,101` + `writer.go:16`). Nothing materializes `Peer.SSHArgs` without crossing it.\n- **Arity re-derived from the live OpenSSH 10.2p1 binary**, not from the source comment. Tables match.\n- **63 adversarial argv through `loadConfigDocument`**, including 23 option names the producer never enumerated — `ProxyJump`, `-J`, `SetEnv`, `PKCS11Provider`, `RemoteCommand`, `ControlMaster`, `PubkeyAuthentication=no`, `RevokedHostKeys=/dev/null`, `PubkeyAcceptedAlgorithms=+ssh-rsa`, `FingerprintHash=md5`… all refused.\n- **Name-parsing divergence attacked directly** (quoted keyword, newline injection, second directive inside one `-o`, unicode separators). No spelling makes AX read a permitted name where ssh reads a dangerous one.\n- **Admitted side verified against the binary:** `ssh -G -F/tmp/cfg h` sets `proxycommand`; `ssh -G -i -F/tmp/cfg h` does not. The `-i` optarg swallow is faithful getopt, not a hole.\n- **Five single-clause narrowing mutants I ran myself** (permit `-F`; `stricthostkeychecking` permits `no`; declare `proxycommand`; group walk ignores non-leading letters — which reintroduces the exact reported `-vo` bypass; admit bare operands). Each reddens cases naming its own clause. Control green, tree clean before and after. No delete-only mutant.\n\n## Gates re-run here, real exit codes\n\n| Gate | Exit |\n| --- | ---: |\n| `go build ./...` | 0 |\n| `go vet ./...` | 0 |\n| `gofmt -l .` | 0 (no output) |\n| `go test ./... -count=1` | 0 (9/9 ok) |\n| `go test ./... -cover -count=1` | 0 |\n| `tracecheck` / `tracecheck -section 6.3` | 0 / 0 |\n| `cataloggen -check` | 0 |\n\n`internal/config` coverage 93.9%.\n\n## Three non-blocking findings for the orchestrator\n\n1. **`LOGBOOK.md` names commit `7eac813`** — unreachable from HEAD, different tree (`964d44e` vs delivered `7fce177`). The producer re-committed as `150040f`. Fix the SHA at checkpoint; the SHA can't be known inside the commit carrying it, so this isn't rework.\n2. **`parseSSHConfigOption` splits the name on any `unicode.IsSpace`** while OpenSSH splits on ASCII whitespace/quote/`=`, so `-o \"BatchMode<U+00A0>yes\"` is admitted by AX and rejected by ssh. One-directional — the name is truncated then must be in the registry, so no dangerous keyword reaches the permitted set. Startup error, not a relaxed host check.\n3. **`UserKnownHostsFile`/`GlobalKnownHostsFile` refused for every value**, stricter than §6.3's \"empty\". Spec-conformant (the §6.3 example argv still loads); flagged so a future custom-known-hosts request is a deliberate registry widening with both-direction samples.\n\nFull evidence attached as `BUG-260902-beqfwr_review-verdict.md`.","ttft_ms":4171,"type":"result","duration_ms":744780,"uuid":"3929a83f-3c75-4723-a93c-b7fd9d58c6af","ttft_stream_ms":3659,"time_to_request_ms":14,"queued_turn_count":0}
